# Conflict and Consensus in the Historical Process: The Intellectual Foundations of the School Finance Reform Litigation Movement.

**Authors:** Ward, James Gordon

## Abstract
Examines development of the equalization idea in American public education, discusses theorists' applications of equalization to school finance, reviews the literature on school-finance reform-litigation effects, and concludes that U.S. history has not strongly supported equalization of educational opportunities. Education is not a fundamental constitutional right in some states. (74 footnotes) (MLH)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ568581

